---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/ui/ComparisonTable.astro';
import FAQSection from '../../components/ui/FAQSection.astro';
import ProConBox from '../../components/ui/ProConBox.astro';
import { brands } from '../../data/generator-brands';

const brand = brands.find((b) => b.slug === 'cummins')!;
const toc = [
  { id: 'heritage', label: 'Industrial heritage' },
  { id: 'lineup', label: 'QuietConnect lineup' },
  { id: 'warranty', label: 'Shorter warranty, honestly' },
  { id: 'verdict', label: 'Who it suits' },
  { id: 'faq', label: 'FAQ' },
];
---
<ArticleLayout
  title="Cummins QuietConnect Standby Generators: Honest Review"
  description="Independent Cummins QuietConnect review: 13–20 kW lineup, uniform 65 dB noise, −40°F rating, short standard warranty, and who should shortlist it."
  category="Brands" categoryHref="/brands/" updated="2026-10-03" readingTime="6 min read" toc={toc}
  sources={[
    { label: 'Cummins — QuietConnect Series', href: 'https://www.cummins.com/en-in/na/generators/home-standby/quietconnect-series', type: 'Manufacturer', verified: 'Oct 2026' },
    { label: 'Generac — Residential Standby Lineup', href: 'https://www.generac.com/residential-products/standby-generators/', type: 'Manufacturer', verified: 'Oct 2026' },
    { label: 'U.S. EIA — Electricity Data Browser', href: 'https://www.eia.gov/electricity/', type: 'Government', verified: 'Oct 2026' },
  ]}
  related={[
    { href: '/brands/kohler/', title: 'Kohler Standby Generators', description: 'Premium alternative.', category: 'Brands' },
    { href: '/brands/champion/', title: 'Champion Standby Generators', description: 'Value alternative.', category: 'Brands' },
  ]}
  prev={{ href: '/brands/champion/', label: 'Champion Brand Guide' }}
  next={{ href: '/comparisons/generac-vs-kohler/', label: 'Generac vs Kohler' }}
>
  <section id="heritage"><h2>Industrial heritage (Onan lineage)</h2>
  <p>Cummins (founded 1919, Columbus, Indiana) powers everything from RVs (Onan) to data centers. QuietConnect is its residential standby line — sound-insulated, weather-protective enclosures with industrial-service DNA and fewer residential storefronts than Generac.</p></section>
  <section id="lineup"><h2>QuietConnect lineup: one noise number</h2>
  <ComparisonTable caption="QuietConnect models" headers={['Model', 'Capacity', 'Noise', 'Notes']} rows={brand.models.map((m) => [m.series, m.capacityKw, m.noiseDb ?? '—', m.notes ?? '—'])} />
  <p class="mt-3">Uniform 65 dB(A) at 23 ft across the line (manufacturer "best-in-class" claim), cold-rated to −40°F, natural gas or propane. The RS20AC bundles the ATS.</p></section>
  <section id="warranty"><h2>Shorter warranty, stated plainly</h2><p>{brand.warranty} This is the thinnest standard coverage in the comparison set — price it accordingly and read the extended terms before signing. A great unit with weak warranty backup needs a great dealer to compensate.</p></section>
  <section id="verdict"><h2>Who QuietConnect suits</h2>
  <ProConBox pros={['Uniform 65 dB; strong cold-weather rating', 'Industrial build and service culture', 'Tight 13–20 kW focus, no bloat']} cons={['Short 2-year standard warranty', 'Fewer residential dealers; caps at 20 kW', 'Less pricing transparency']} prosTitle="Strengths" consTitle="Watch-outs" />
  <p class="mt-4">Shortlist for cold climates and noise-sensitive lots where a Cummins servicer is genuinely local — especially 13–20 kW essentials-to-mid homes.</p></section>
  <section id="faq"><span class="sr-only">FAQ anchor</span></section>
  <FAQSection items={[
    { q: 'Are Cummins home generators quiet?', a: 'QuietConnect models are uniformly rated 65 dB(A) at 23 ft with insulated enclosures — competitive, though rivals publish quieter flagship numbers (e.g., Kohler 26RCA 56 dB, Champion 8.5 kW 59.5 dB).' },
    { q: 'Why is the Cummins warranty so short?', a: 'The 2-year residential standard reflects its industrial quoting culture; a 5-year extended exists (parts only after year 2). Factor extended coverage into price comparisons.' },
    { q: 'Cummins vs Generac for cold climates?', a: 'Cummins −40°F rating is a documented edge for extreme-cold regions; Generac counters with denser cold-region dealer coverage. Weight whichever your ZIP code actually supports.' },
  
    { q: 'What does QuietConnect mean in practice?', a: 'Sound-insulated, weather-protective enclosures tuned for a uniform 65 dB(A) across the 13–20 kW line — no loud outlier in the family.' },
    { q: 'Who services Cummins residential units?', a: 'Cummins distributors and certified dealers — industrial-service DNA with fewer residential storefronts. Confirm one near you before committing.' },
    { q: 'Is Cummins worth it over Generac?', a: 'For extreme cold or noise-sensitive lots with a local Cummins servicer: yes. For everywhere else, weigh the 2-year standard warranty honestly against the price.' },
  ]} />
  <section id="conclusion"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Industrial-grade quiet and cold-weather chops with warranty fine print to respect. Next: <a href="/comparisons/generac-vs-kohler/">the big comparison</a> or <a href="/cost/standby-generator-cost/">installed costs</a>.</p></section>
</ArticleLayout>
